1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,600
Welcome to Pocketful Factory, our submission for the WeAreDevelopers and BAND Dark Factory hackathon.

2
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:15,062
In this challenge, our goal was to build a complete bitemporal financial settlement engine without human developers writing any business logic.

3
00:00:15,062 --> 00:00:22,425
Inside Band Desktop, we established three distinct agent seats: Architect, Coder, and Auditor.

4
00:00:22,425 --> 00:00:27,762
Each seat operates under a generic mandate with strict separation of concerns.

5
00:00:27,762 --> 00:00:31,187
The operator initiates the project from the room.

6
00:00:31,187 --> 00:00:38,275
The Architect verifies state invariants, defines interface contracts, and hands off tasks to the Coder.

7
00:00:38,275 --> 00:00:49,212
When tasks complete, the Auditor performs rigorous verification against edge cases and reports findings back in the room, fulfilling the reciprocal messaging requirements of Gate 2.

8
00:00:49,372 --> 00:00:52,472
Here is our official harness verification.

9
00:00:52,422 --> 00:00:57,134
All offline static gates pass cleanly with zero track leaks.

10
00:00:57,134 --> 00:01:07,084
Running the multi-stage evaluation across all four stages, our service achieves a one-hundred percent pass rate across all one hundred and ninety-three conformance tests.

11
00:01:07,084 --> 00:01:13,672
With zero regressions and zero manual workarounds, our factory successfully claims Stage 4.

12
00:01:13,828 --> 00:01:19,078
Now let's examine the generated web client running against our Stage 4 server.

13
00:01:19,028 --> 00:01:21,253
We sign in as Ada.

14
00:01:21,253 --> 00:01:25,965
The dashboard displays the real-time available balance and active holds.

15
00:01:25,965 --> 00:01:37,078
When transferring 10 Euros to Bob, the client performs an optimistic update, enforces client idempotency to prevent double-spending, and records the transfer in the activity feed.

16
00:01:37,078 --> 00:01:44,565
Navigating to statements, our bitemporal ledger maintains truthful historical records with exact balance reconciliation.

17
00:01:44,565 --> 00:01:48,728
Every stage builds cleanly from an isolated container.

18
00:01:48,728 --> 00:01:50,740
Thank you for watching!

